FORECAST DATA
-------------

NOAA Global Forecast System (GFS) Wave model data
  Source: U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA)
          National Centers for Environmental Prediction (NCEP)
  Access:  https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/
  Notes:   U.S. Government work. This project downloads GRIB2 files via HTTPS.
           Users of derived forecast maps should not treat them as official
           NOAA/NWS products. See NOAA and NWS terms of use for data policies.


NOAA Global Forecast System (GFS) Atmosphere model data
  Source: NOAA / NCEP
  Access:  https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/
  Notes:   Precipitation, temperature, humidity, and MSLP fields used for Map
           and Site Forecast atmosphere products.


HYCOM ocean model data
  Source: Hybrid Coordinate Ocean Model / Naval Research Laboratory
  Access:  https://tds.hycom.org/
  Notes:   Sea-surface temperature and surface currents via NCSS.


Astronomical tide harmonics
  Preferred: FES2022 (AVISO / CNES / LEGOS / CLS)
  Bootstrap: GOT4.10 (NASA GSFC)
  Software:  pyTMD (https://github.com/pyTMD/pyTMD)
  Notes:     Site Forecast tide charts are harmonic reconstructions only and
             do not include storm surge or residual water level. Cite AVISO
             FES terms when publishing FES2022-derived products.


Historical AIS (optional lane harvest)
  Source:  AISDataPortal/DB on Hugging Face
  Access:  https://huggingface.co/datasets/AISDataPortal/DB
  Notes:   Used only by the offline `scripts/build_route_graph.py --source ais`
           builder. The committed lane graph ships from hand-digitized corridors
           unless an AIS harvest validates full port connectivity. Not used in
           the per-cycle forecast pipeline.


